@Adar195 essentially, institutions trade with such large amounts of volume, now I'm sure you understand, for every buyer there needs to be a seller, vice versa. Now institutions cannot trade as regular, as there's no participant willing to buy or sell their moves, so essentially, institutions have to manipulate the market, stopping out all retail members, which in return creates liquidity, and this liquidity is basically like a key which gives them access to make their next move...

If you do not know what I mean by institutions and retail, a quick Google search will do the trick.

God bless 🙏🏽
